    "scope_review": "The generic theorem identifies matrix multiplication in the existing ArchiveCochainBasis with the supplied-weight function operator. The original source pin db3091aded8f6cfe8d39dcd973ccf30ec40dfb08 contains the isolated 2x2 obstruction; the full-carrier transfer is a separate branch formalization delta at c3ceba511bab5c435d715fd56382615fc1dc1505. The exact L=4 application proves the vacuum and B-singleton action equations and applies that conditional transfer. The supplied positive form and self-adjointness premise are not physically derived. The all-even extension requires an even archive period N+2 and proves the same full-carrier block and conditional obstruction there; it is separate from the Eq. (5) Fourier application. The signed scalar second-order operator now has an all-size character eigenbasis, a complete scalar site Fourier inversion, and an injective sixteen-label Fock coefficient embedding per momentum. A companion module defines the explicitly role-signed first-order CAR operator and proves its square equals that operator on the full carrier; composition gives the Eq. (5) all-size squared-mode law for every Fock profile. Its direct first-order Fourier action is now an explicit finite CAR map on each Fock profile, and the induced map squares to the same symbol. This does not make an arbitrary profile a first-order eigenvector; physical action/source selection and GR closure remain open."
